};
var PS_HELP = {
  job: {
    title: '1 · Connect to an MTX job',
    what: '<p>Optional. Loads a job\'s subject wells, its saved Torque &amp; Drag models and the survey versions of the chosen well. Without a job you can still enter a string and import a survey from Excel.</p>',
    how: '<p><b>Well / leg</b> lists the real wells only. <b>Survey version (start from)</b> lists the uploaded survey and every corrected version saved from it (e.g. "… SAG …"); the banner shows the corrections already applied. A version that already has a PipeStretch correction cannot be stretched again. Each station keeps its <b>original (tally) MD</b>, which is what places it in a BHA run.</p>' +
      '<p><b>Use saved T&amp;D string + parameters</b> copies the chosen T&amp;D scenario: string, casing program, friction factors, WOB, mud weight, and its hole sections and BHA runs (used by "Use T&amp;D runs"). <b>📄 Chain QC report</b> summarises every correction of the selected version [CHAIN].</p>',
    why: '<p>T&amp;D is the master source of BHAs, runs and sections, so the stretch is computed with the same string the T&amp;D module models, and corrections can be chained (e.g. PipeStretch → SAG) on one auditable history.</p>',
    src: ['TD', 'CHAIN']
  },
  string: {
    title: '2 · Drill string and T&D runs',
    what: '<p>The string from the bit up (same table as the T&amp;D modeler) and, optionally, the T&amp;D BHA runs.</p>',
    how: '<p><b>SurQC model:</b> rows from the bit that end within the BHA length are the BHA (steel, mass and area averaged over its length); everything above is drill pipe with the single DP OD/ID entered here [SQC; SM].</p>' +
      '<p><b>T&amp;D model:</b> the whole table is the string, as the T&amp;D modeler uses it (Wt column; above the last row its default 4½" DP) [TD].</p>' +
      '<p><b>Use T&amp;D runs</b> (T&amp;D model only): a survey at MD s was taken with the bit at <i>original MD + sensor offset</i>; the station uses the run whose bit-MD range contains that depth (deepest start wins if two overlap; shallower than the first run → first run) — the rule of the T&amp;D Hookload calculation. That run\'s string, top drill pipe, hole section, casing set by then, mud weight and friction factors come from the T&amp;D module\'s own run setup [TD]. Stations below every run are left uncorrected and flagged. "Top DP = default 4½"" means the run has no drill-pipe rows in T&amp;D.</p>',
    why: '<p>Stretch depends on the pipe area and weight along the whole string, so the drill pipe matters as much as the BHA. Each run drilled with its own string, so one string for the whole well is only an approximation.</p>',
    src: ['SQC', 'TD', 'SM']
  },
  analysis: {
    title: '3 · Stretch analysis — SurQC vs T&D',
    what: '<p>Computes the MD correction at every survey station: <b>mechanical</b> stretch (tension) + <b>thermal</b> expansion (temperature), shown separately and as total.</p>' +
      '<table class="hp-tbl"><tr><th></th><th>SurQC</th><th>T&amp;D</th></tr>' +
      '<tr><td>What it is</td><td>Port of SurQC\'s stretch correction (element core identical to the C#)</td><td>Tension from MTX\'s soft-string T&amp;D model</td></tr>' +
      '<tr><td>Tension</td><td>One profile, bit at the last survey MD, used for every station</td><td>Solved per station, bit at station MD + sensor offset</td></tr>' +
      '<tr><td>Friction / geometry</td><td>μ = 0.25, inclination only</td><td>Azimuth, cased / open-hole friction factors, casing program, hole sections</td></tr>' +
      '<tr><td>String</td><td>BHA (averaged) + one DP size, steel</td><td>Full string, per component; T&amp;D runs optional</td></tr>' +
      '<tr><td>Thermal</td><td>α × gradient × TVD per 1 m element (pipe calibrated at surface temperature)</td><td>α ∫(T − T<sub>cal</sub>) dMD, T = T<sub>surface</sub> + gradient × TVD</td></tr></table>',
    how: '<p><b>SurQC</b> [SQC; SM]: survey interpolated on 1 m elements (minimum-curvature arc). Element mass = steel volume × (7700 − ρ<sub>mud</sub>). Tension built from the bit (0) upward:</p>' +
      '<p class="hp-eq">along = m·g·cos(I<sub>avg</sub>), side = m·g·sin(I<sub>avg</sub>)<br>thrust = −2·T<sub>below</sub>·sin(½·½(I<sub>above</sub> − I)), drag = 0.25·|thrust − side|<br>T = T<sub>below</sub> + along ± drag &nbsp;(+ pulling out, 0 static, − running in)<br>mechanical per element = T/(A·E), E = 210 GPa; thermal per element = 12×10⁻⁶ /°C × gradient × TVD</p>' +
      '<p>MD correction at a station = stretch accumulated from surface, interpolated between the two nearest 1 m points. SurQC quirks kept on purpose: quarter of the inclination change in the thrust, no azimuth, BHA bottom at the last survey MD, steel only.</p>' +
      '<p><b>T&amp;D</b> [JFD; TD; SM]: effective tension F along the string from the T&amp;D soft-string model for the chosen load case, with the bit at station MD + sensor offset. Mechanical stretch of the pipe above the station [HOOKE]:</p>' +
      '<p class="hp-eq">ΔL<sub>mech</sub> = ∫<sub>0</sub><sup>MD</sup> F/(E·A) dMD &nbsp;&nbsp; ΔL<sub>th</sub> = α ∫<sub>0</sub><sup>MD</sup> (T(x) − T<sub>cal</sub>) dMD, &nbsp;T(x) = T<sub>surface</sub> + gradient × TVD(x)</p>' +
      '<p>A from each component\'s OD/ID, trapezoid between the 10 m T&amp;D nodes. The thermal term is the ISCWSA eBook correction (coefficient × length × (mean temperature − calibration temperature)) integrated along the string [EB]; with T<sub>cal</sub> = T<sub>surface</sub> it reduces to SurQC\'s α·G·TVD per metre. α default 12×10⁻⁶ /°C (SurQC\'s value) — the eBook quotes both 1.3 m per 1000 m per 100 °C (13×10⁻⁶ /°C, §15.2) and ~8.6×10⁻⁶ ft/ft/°F (15.5×10⁻⁶ /°C, p.103), so enter your pipe\'s value if known.</p>',
    why: '<p>Pipe stretch and thermal expansion make the true depth of the sensor deeper than the pipe tally. The error grows with depth and tension and is systematic, so it shifts TVD and positions along the whole well [EB]. Use <b>SurQC</b> to reproduce SurQC; use <b>T&amp;D</b> for the string, friction and runs as modelled in the T&amp;D module.</p>',
    src: ['SQC', 'JFD', 'EB', 'HOOKE', 'TD', 'SM']
  },
  survey: {
    title: '4 · Stretch-corrected survey',
    what: '<p>The survey with the total stretch added to each MD, the run used, and the recomputed TVD / N / E.</p>',
    how: '<p class="hp-eq">Corrected MD = measured MD + (mechanical + thermal) &nbsp;&nbsp; Inc, Az unchanged</p><p>Positions by minimum curvature [BOU]. <b>Save as new version</b> creates a new well version "&lt;well&gt; [earlier corrections+]STRETCH &lt;date&gt;" with the correction history (per-station ΔMD); the starting version is never modified [CHAIN]. <b>📄 Report</b> prints the inputs, runs, method, plot, corrected survey and the corrections applied before this one.</p>',
    why: '<p>The saved version is the starting point for the next correction (e.g. SAG), which still assigns BHA runs by the original tally MD.</p>',
    src: ['BOU', 'CHAIN', 'SM']
  },
  plot: {
    title: 'Stretch along the well',
    what: '<p>Mechanical, thermal and total MD correction at each survey station, against measured depth.</p>',
    how: '<p>Values of the corrected-survey table (section 4). With T&amp;D runs a change of run can show as a step (different string, mud or hole) [TD; SM].</p>',
    why: '<p>Shows which term dominates and where: thermal grows steadily with depth; mechanical follows the tension, so it depends on the string weight, friction and load case.</p>',
    src: ['SM', 'TD']
  }
};
function openPsHelp(key){
  var h = PS_HELP[key]; if(!h) return;
  document.getElementById('hpTitle').innerHTML = h.title;
  document.getElementById('hpBody').innerHTML = '<h4>What you are looking at</h4>' + h.what + '<h4>How it is calculated</h4>' + h.how + '<h4>Why it matters</h4>' + h.why +
    '<h4>Sources</h4><ol class="hp-src">' + h.src.map(function(k){ return '<li><strong>[' + k + ']</strong> ' + PS_SRC[k] + '</li>'; }).join('') + '</ol>';
  document.getElementById('hpModal').classList.add('open');
}
function closePsHelp(){ document.getElementById('hpModal').classList.remove('open'); }
document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){ if(e.key === 'Escape') closePsHelp(); });
(function(){
  function btn(key, cls){ var b = document.createElement('button'); b.type = 'button'; b.className = 'pp-help' + (cls ? ' ' + cls : ''); b.textContent = '?'; b.title = 'About this';
    b.onclick = function(ev){ ev.stopPropagation(); openPsHelp(key); }; return b; }
  var secs = { '1 ·': 'job', '2 ·': 'string', '3 ·': 'analysis', '4 ·': 'survey' };
  document.querySelectorAll('.panel > h2').forEach(function(h){ var t = h.textContent.trim();
    Object.keys(secs).forEach(function(p){ if(t.indexOf(p) === 0){ h.style.display = 'flex'; h.style.alignItems = 'center'; h.appendChild(btn(secs[p])); } }); });
  var el = document.getElementById('plot');
  if(el){ var w = document.createElement('div'); w.style.position = 'relative'; el.parentNode.insertBefore(w, el); w.appendChild(el); w.appendChild(btn('plot', 'pp-help-plot')); }
})();
</script>
